# Paths that DO NOT affect the e2e suite but DO affect the production
# runtime. When the only changes in a push are paths matched by
# `.ci-ignore` OR this file, CD skips the e2e step but still runs
# deploy + canary — the canary catches anything the skip missed.
#
# Syntax: POSIX extended regex (egrep), one pattern per line. Same
# parser as `.ci-ignore`. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are
# ignored.
#
# Be CONSERVATIVE — only add paths that the e2e suite genuinely cannot
# exercise. Examples of paths that LOOK skip-safe but aren't:
#   src/runtime/home-config.ts — covered by unit tests, but a behavior
#     change should still run e2e to catch downstream effects.
#   Dockerfile / sandbox/Dockerfile — sandbox image is exercised by e2e.

# Per-channel home routing. tests/e2e/helpers.ts:setupTempDataDir
# overrides AGENT_HOMES_CONFIG with a per-run file:// config, so the
# committed file is bypassed during e2e.
^config/homes\.json$

# Prod-only Fly app config.
^fly\.toml$

# Production-only Slack app manifests. e2e uses the dedicated agenta-ci
# / agenta-tester apps, whose manifests aren't in this repo.
^slack-manifests/.*\.json$

# Scripts that only run after e2e (deploy + canary) or are operator
# tools never invoked by tests.
^scripts/deploy-bot-fly\.ts$
^scripts/canary\.ts$
